# Static DHCP reservations for the router's dnsmasq (dhcp-hostsfile).
#
# Format: one reservation per line, "MAC,hostname[,IP]" (no IP just pins
# the hostname/DNS name for a device without reserving a fixed address -
# see the printer below). A comment line ('#...') directly above an entry,
# with no blank line between them, is treated as that entry's note by
# scripts/dhcp-static.sh; a blank line breaks that association. dnsmasq
# itself ignores blank lines and comment lines outright.
#
# This file only seeds /var/lib/dnsmasq/static-hosts.conf the FIRST time
# the router boots with that file missing (systemd.tmpfiles 'C' rule in
# modules/dhcp-dns.nix only copies when the destination doesn't already
# exist) - so it's the baseline restored on a full reimage, not a live
# mirror of the router's current reservations. Manage the live file with
# scripts/dhcp-static.sh (installed on the router itself) instead of
# editing it directly - that tool handles conflict checks and reloading
# dnsmasq for you. If you want this seed to reflect reservations added
# that way, copy /var/lib/dnsmasq/static-hosts.conf back into this file
# by hand and redeploy.
#
# Carried over from OPNsense's opt5 dhcpd staticmaps during the original
# migration to this router - see git history of this file for that
# context.

# HP LaserJet Printer - no static IP in source config either
